[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The renderer may know the shape of a view and never its content

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-VIEW-RENDERER-IS-CONTENT-BLIND
TITLE: The renderer may know the shape of a view and never its content
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The renderer knows the wireline schema, the widget words and how to draw
each, the legend's colour vocabulary, and that a narrative is placed as its
PLACE declares and drawn as its WIDGET names over the subject its Over relation
names. It knows no UID, no tag word, no node-type name, no plan directory and
no reading of one type through another. Every word on the page comes from the
payload: from a narrative's own fields, or from a table a backed script
computed from the export. A renderer edit that is needed to show a new node, a
new word or a new project violates this -- and so does a renderer that derives
structure from the shape of the tree instead of from what the narratives
declare.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The operator's line: "the renderer can have opinions on the data it expects
to render ... the line is if the renderer needs any awareness of the
content." A renderer that knows content is a second, unreviewed copy of the
canon, which is what the one-off render's hand-written headlines were.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-VIEWS-ARE-REGENERABLE
  ROLE: Governed_By
